00:07:23.547 --> 00:07:26.140
Yeah, so basically,

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.040
the basic components
of a cell culture room

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.673
are the incubator,

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.477
the hood where you work
to keep things sterile,

00:07:34.477 --> 00:07:35.583
and your microscope.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:45.290
So we're gonna head back to
the other cell culture room

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:50.290
where I'm gonna actually get some cells

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.220
that I'm gonna be able to show you guys.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:56.417
So as I said, this is the hood.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:08.170
And basically, it works
by you raising up the sash

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:11.030
and then you can work inside of it.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:14.360
And inside is sterile,
outside's not sterile.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.604
This is how we prevent
ourselves from getting bacteria

00:08:17.604 --> 00:08:20.193
(indistinct) contamination.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.220
We grow our cells in an incubator.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:26.270
So this is an incubator.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:30.000
We keep it at 37 degrees Celsius,

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.240
which is about 98.7 degrees
Fahrenheit or body temperature.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.073
So basically,

00:08:35.073 --> 00:08:37.490
these cells are used to
growing in a human body,

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.490
so we keep them at the same temperature.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:41.913
So you can see,

00:08:41.913 --> 00:08:45.190
we have a whole lot of
