00:36:58.350 --> 00:36:59.930
and there are some programs

00:36:59.930 --> 00:37:03.540
where high school students
can join a lab for the summer

00:37:03.540 --> 00:37:04.380
and they learn.

00:37:04.380 --> 00:37:07.540
And I guess, I can mostly
speak from biology.

00:37:07.540 --> 00:37:09.490
I can't speak of other sciences

00:37:09.490 --> 00:37:11.858
'cause that's not what
my experience is in.

00:37:11.858 --> 00:37:15.230
But I think you either
as a high school student

00:37:15.230 --> 00:37:16.930
or as an undergrad,

00:37:16.930 --> 00:37:19.350
a lot of people do it as an undergrad,

00:37:19.350 --> 00:37:22.340
getting into a lab either via the summer

00:37:22.340 --> 00:37:24.470
or during the semester,

00:37:24.470 --> 00:37:26.470
there's a whole bunch
of different programs

00:37:26.470 --> 00:37:31.470
at various research
institutions at universities,

00:37:32.427 --> 00:37:34.320
applying for those.

00:37:34.320 --> 00:37:36.113
Or once you go to college,

00:37:37.520 --> 00:37:39.400
like you're in biology 101,

00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:40.800
you can go talk to your professor

00:37:40.800 --> 00:37:42.940
and be like, hey, I want to do research.

00:37:42.940 --> 00:37:45.990
Like, do you have any suggestions
on who I should talk to,

00:37:45.990 --> 00:37:49.193
or you know, what lab I
might be able to join?

00:37:50.069 --> 00:37:53.880
Also, as was pointed out in the chat,

00:37:53.880 --> 00:37:57.398
RockEDU has a lot of great programs

00:37:57.398 --> 00:38:02.398
