00:38:15.250 --> 00:38:17.030
and I was like, hey,
can I come work for you?

00:38:17.030 --> 00:38:18.110
And he didn't have room,

00:38:18.110 --> 00:38:20.075
but he passed my email on to somebody else

00:38:20.075 --> 00:38:21.630
and they did have room.

00:38:21.630 --> 00:38:24.600
And so I ended up in a lab that way.

00:38:24.600 --> 00:38:28.530
And it was such a really
cool, great experience.

00:38:28.530 --> 00:38:30.600
I think the earlier you
can start, the better,

00:38:30.600 --> 00:38:32.810
but it's also never too late to start.

00:38:32.810 --> 00:38:37.436
So, I mean, it's all about exploring.

00:38:37.436 --> 00:38:40.130
I've done research in a
bunch of different topics.

00:38:40.130 --> 00:38:43.010
I did plant research for a
year while I was an undergrad

00:38:43.010 --> 00:38:46.140
and I quickly learned that I
didn't want to study plants.

00:38:46.140 --> 00:38:48.180
And so I think just trying things,

00:38:48.180 --> 00:38:51.460
figuring out what field
you're interested in.

00:38:51.460 --> 00:38:52.880
For me, it's cancer biology.

00:38:52.880 --> 00:38:54.950
I like trying to understand

00:38:54.950 --> 00:38:59.660
how these cells take what
happens during normal development

00:38:59.660 --> 00:39:00.800
and manipulate it,

00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:04.809
and turn it to their own uses.

00:39:04.809 --> 00:39:07.500
But for other people,
it could be immunology.

00:39:07.500 --> 00:39:10.270
It could be material science.

00:39:10.270 --> 00:39:11.490
It could be physics.

00:39:11.490 --> 00:39:14.450
Just finding what research,
if that's the career you want.

00:39:14.450 --> 00:39:16.900
There's also so many other careers.

00:39:16.900 --> 00:39:20.283
So just try things, I think,
would be my biggest advice.

